     "side": "RIGHT",
-    "body": "### Critical Bug: `.run()` Used Instead of `.get()` for Query Returning Row\n**Risk:** In `better-sqlite3`, `stmt.run()` is used for DML operations (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE) and returns a `RunResult` metadata object `{ changes: 0, lastInsertRowid: 0 }`. It does NOT return query row results. In JavaScript, `{ changes: 0, lastInsertRowid: 0 }` is truthy, meaning `!row` will ALWAYS evaluate to `false`.\n\nAs a consequence, `isCallsignAvailable` will return `false` for every single callsign check across the application. All profile callsign updates and registrations will fail and incorrectly declare names as taken (`CALLSIGN_TAKEN`).\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\nChange `.run(...)` back to `.get(...)`:\n```typescript\n    const row = db.prepare(\n        `SELECT 1 FROM members WHERE lower(callsign) = ? AND status NOT IN ('migrated', 'pruned') AND public_key != ? LIMIT 1`\n    ).get(norm, excludePublicKey ?? '');\n    return !row;\n```"
-  },
