-    "position": 53,
-    "side": "RIGHT",
-    "body": "### Architectural Risk: DB Index Mismatch with Application Availability Check\n**Risk:** `isCallsignAvailable` was updated to exclude `pruned` members (`status NOT IN ('migrated', 'pruned')`), but the DB partial unique index `idx_members_callsign_unique` in `apps/server/src/db/db.ts` is still defined as:\n`CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_members_callsign_unique ON members(lower(callsign)) WHERE status != 'migrated'`\n\nIf a user reclaims a callsign previously owned by a `pruned` member, `isCallsignAvailable` will report it as available, but the database write will throw an unhandled `SqliteError: UNIQUE constraint failed: members.lower(callsign)` because the database index still includes `pruned` rows.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\nUpdate the partial index definition in `apps/server/src/db/db.ts` to match the application check:\n```sql\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_members_callsign_unique ON members(lower(callsign)) WHERE status NOT IN ('migrated', 'pruned');\n```"
-  },
