-    "path": "apps/native/app/(tabs)/settings.tsx",
-    "position": 657,
-    "side": "RIGHT",
-    "body": "### Edge Case: HTTP Error Responses Caught as Offline Mode\n**Risk:** If the server rejects a profile update with an HTTP error status code (e.g. `400 Bad Request` for invalid parameters or `CALLSIGN_TOO_SHORT`), `if (!res.ok)` throws an `Error`. This error is immediately caught by the inner `catch` block on line 663, which logs a warning, alerts `\"Offline Mode\"`, sets `pending_profile_sync`, and then proceeds to execute the local state update (`updateMemberProfile` & `updateCallsign`) with the rejected callsign.\n\nInvalid or rejected callsigns will be persisted locally on the device and queued for endless re-sync attempts.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\nDifferentiate between network connection failures and HTTP client/server error responses:\n```typescript\n                    if (res.status === 409) {\n                        Alert.alert('Name Taken', 'That name is already taken in this community. Please pick another.');\n                        return;\n                    }\n                    if (!res.ok) {\n                        const errData = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\n                        Alert.alert('Update Failed', errData.message || 'Server rejected the profile update.');\n                        return;\n                    }\n```"
+    "body": "### UX & Copywriting\n**Risk:** `TERMINAL_REFUSALS` includes `'NOT_FOUND'`, but `reversalMemo` matches on `'RECEIPT_NOT_FOUND'`. When a terminal reversal occurs with reason `'NOT_FOUND'` and no custom `outcome.message` is supplied, `reversalMemo` falls through to generic fallback copy (`'Refunded — this cross-community purchase could not be completed'`) instead of explaining that the other community did not complete the sale. Similarly, `'BAD_SIGNATURE'` and `'RECEIPT_MISMATCH'` lack specific memo entries.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\nUpdate `reversalMemo` to include `'NOT_FOUND'`, `'BAD_SIGNATURE'`, and `'RECEIPT_MISMATCH'`:\n```typescript\nfunction reversalMemo(reason: string): string {\n    switch (reason) {\n        case 'CAPACITY_LAPSED':\n            return 'Refunded — the other community had reached its credit limit';\n        case 'NOT_FOUND':\n        case 'RECEIPT_NOT_FOUND':\n            return 'Refunded — the other community did not complete the sale';\n        case 'BAD_SIGNATURE':\n        case 'RECEIPT_MISMATCH':\n            return 'Refunded — invalid transaction verification from peer community';\n        default:\n            return 'Refunded — this cross-community purchase could not be completed';\n    }\n}\n```"
