+    "path": "apps/server/src/state-engine.ts",
+    "position": 2678,
+    "side": "RIGHT",
+    "body": "### Consequences & Impact\n**Risk:** `adminPruneUser` executes within a synchronous `db.transaction()` block. `payFromCommons()` and `moveToCommons()` directly mutate in-memory `ledger` account balances and the global `COMMONS_BALANCE`. If a failure occurs later in the transaction (e.g. during `UPDATE posts` or `adminSetUserStatus`), SQLite rolls back the database writes, but the in-memory `ledger` state and `COMMONS_BALANCE` remain mutated. This desynchronizes in-memory balances from persisted SQLite state, violating the zero-sum invariant until node restart.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```typescript\nexport function adminPruneUser(publicKey: string) {\n    const commonsBefore = getCommonsBalanceExact();\n    try {\n        db.transaction(() => {\n            const account = ledger.getAccount(publicKey);\n            const balance = account.balance;\n\n            if (balance < 0) {\n                const D = Math.abs(balance);\n                payFromCommons(publicKey, D, `Settle bad debt for pruned user: ${publicKey}`, { allowDeficit: true });\n            } else if (balance > 0) {\n                moveToCommons(publicKey, balance, `Confiscate credit for pruned user: ${publicKey}`,\n                    { allowMemberDebit: true });\n            }\n\n            adminSetUserStatus(publicKey, 'pruned');\n            db.prepare(\"UPDATE posts SET status='cancelled', active=0 WHERE author_pubkey=? AND status IN ('active', 'pending')\").run(publicKey);\n        })();\n    } catch (err) {\n        setCommonsBalance(commonsBefore);\n        reconcileLedgerFromDb();\n        throw err;\n    }\n    broadcast({ type: 'user_pruned', publicKey });\n}\n```"
+  },
+  {
+    "path": "apps/server/src/state-engine.ts",
+    "position": 1241,
+    "side": "RIGHT",
+    "body": "### Consequences & Impact\n**Risk:** `moveToCommons()` throws an unhandled `Error` if `from` is an ordinary member account and `opts?.allowMemberDebit` is omitted. In route handlers or background job callers expecting `moveToCommons()` to return `null` on failure (similar to `transfer()`), an unhandled exception will cause HTTP 500 server errors or uncaught promise rejections instead of clean error responses.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```typescript\n    if (!synthetic && !treasury && !opts?.allowMemberDebit) {\n        console.error(`[moveToCommons] Rejected: account ${from} is neither synthetic nor a treasury`);\n        return null;\n    }\n```"
+  },
