+    "path": "apps/server/src/routes/treasury.ts",
+    "position": 238,
+    "side": "RIGHT",
+    "body": "### Consequences & Impact\n**Risk:** The sweep route delegates balance movement to `moveToCommons()`. While `moveToCommons()` successfully preserves the zero-sum invariant by mutating `COMMONS_BALANCE` directly instead of transferring to the shadow `COMMONS_POOL` account row, calling `moveToCommons()` without wrapping it in a safety check or exception handler leaves the route vulnerable if `moveToCommons()` throws an exception on non-treasury or invalid keys.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```typescript\n        let ok: Transaction | null = null;\n        try {\n            ok = moveToCommons(treasury, amt, `Surplus swept to Commons from ${treasury.slice(0, 8)}`);\n        } catch (e: any) {\n            ctx.status = 400;\n            ctx.body = { error: e.message || 'Sweep failed' };\n            return;\n        }\n        if (!ok) {\n            ctx.status = 400;\n            ctx.body = { error: 'That sweep could not be completed — check the treasury still holds this amount.' };\n            return;\n        }\n```"
