+    "position": 81,
+    "side": "RIGHT",
+    "body": "### Critical Issue: Missing `await` on Asynchronous Stream Write\n**Risk:** Removing `await` from `stream.send(encoder.encode(data))` causes `await stream.close()` to execute concurrently while the write operation is still in-flight. In libp2p, closing a stream while `send()` is pending introduces a race condition where the stream write side is closed or flushed before `stream.send()` finishes transmitting data. This can result in truncated payload transmission, network protocol write errors, or unhandled promise rejections if `stream.send()` fails. Downstream, this risks corrupting or failing settlement protocol exchanges (`settle_purchase`, `settle_receipt`, `settle_receipt_status`).\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```typescript\nasync function writeToStream(stream: any, data: string): Promise<void> {\n    await stream.send(encoder.encode(data));\n    await stream.close();\n}\n```"
+  },
+  {
+    "path": "apps/server/src/handshake.ts",
+    "position": 98,
+    "side": "RIGHT",
+    "body": "### Critical Issue: Missing `await` on Asynchronous Stream Write\n**Risk:** Removing `await` from `stream.send(encoder.encode(data))` in `writeToStream` allows `await stream.close()` to execute immediately while `stream.send()` is still processing asynchronously. In node-to-node handshakes, this race condition can lead to remote peers receiving incomplete handshake JSON payloads or premature EOF signals before the handshake reply is fully transmitted. Consequently, handshake JSON parsing fails on remote nodes, preventing peer discovery and mutual trust establishment. Additionally, any network error during `stream.send()` becomes an unhandled promise rejection.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\n```typescript\nasync function writeToStream(stream: any, data: string): Promise<void> {\n    await stream.send(encoder.encode(data));\n    await stream.close();\n}\n```"
+  }
+]
