+    "body": "### Code Quality & Logic\n**Risk:** Critical demurrage math bug: applying past deferred time intervals to newly changed balances. `applyDecay` returns early (`return account;`) without updating `lastDemurrageEpoch` whenever decay is deferred or below the recording threshold (`<= 0.0001`).\n\nIf an account sat with an old epoch (e.g. at 0 balance or inside the tax-free Green Zone) and then receives a transfer, leaving `lastDemurrageEpoch` untouched means the next read will calculate demurrage on the *new, higher balance* over the *entire past time interval* when the account held 0 or low funds. Mathematically, a deferred interval cannot be applied post-hoc to a modified principal balance without over-taxing new deposits.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\nReset `lastDemurrageEpoch = currentEpoch` during balance mutations (`transfer` and `moveToCommons`) so new funds start their demurrage epoch cleanly at transaction time:\n```typescript\n        const currentEpoch = this.getCurrentEpoch();\n        fromAccount.lastDemurrageEpoch = currentEpoch;\n        toAccount.lastDemurrageEpoch = currentEpoch;\n        return true;\n```"
