+    "body": "### Consequences & Impact\n**Risk:** `loadState` rewinds `COMMONS_BALANCE` by subtracting memory decay events, but ignores `COMMONS_POOL` when it is included in the `accounts` array. When `reconcileLedgerFromDb` is triggered following a raw-SQL mutation on the Commons pool (such as a treasury allocation or community funding payout), `loadState` rewinds unpersisted memory decay against the old `COMMONS_BALANCE` variable rather than accepting the new durable `COMMONS_POOL` balance. When `persistCommonsBalance()` flushes 5 minutes later, it overwrites the DB with the stale in-memory figure, quietly reversing the raw-SQL mutation.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\nCheck if `COMMONS_POOL` is present in the reloaded `accounts` array and synchronize `COMMONS_BALANCE` to it, falling back to memory unwinding only when `COMMONS_POOL` is omitted (e.g., in unit tests):\n```typescript\n    loadState(accounts: LedgerAccount[]): void {\n        const undoneCredit = this.decayEvents.reduce((total, e) => total + e.amount, 0);\n        this.accounts = new Map();\n        let hasCommonsDbRow = false;\n        \n        accounts.forEach(acc => {\n            this.accounts.set(acc.id, acc);\n            if (acc.id === 'COMMONS_POOL') {\n                COMMONS_BALANCE = acc.balance;\n                hasCommonsDbRow = true;\n            }\n        });\n\n        // Only rewind in-memory decay if not synchronizing with a durable DB row\n        if (!hasCommonsDbRow && undoneCredit > 0) {\n            COMMONS_BALANCE -= undoneCredit;\n        }\n        \n        this.decayEvents = [];\n        this.decayCapWarned = false;\n    }\n```"
+  },
+  {
+    "path": "packages/beanpool-core/src/ledger.ts",
+    "position": 170,
+    "side": "RIGHT",
+    "body": "### Consequences & Impact\n**Risk:** Demurrage interval erasure on balance mutations. If an account's decay is deferred (because `decayedAmount <= 0.0001` or `MAX_PENDING_DECAY_EVENTS` is reached), `applyDecay` returns without updating `account.lastDemurrageEpoch`. However, when `getAccount()` was called inside `transfer()` or `moveToCommons()`, those mutating methods unconditionally set `lastDemurrageEpoch = currentEpoch` at the end of the transaction. This permanently advances the epoch marker without decaying the balance, erasing the deferred time interval and under-collecting demurrage for active accounts.\n\n**Suggested Fix:**\nEnsure mutating operations (`transfer()`, `moveToCommons()`) force decay application so the deferred interval is never wiped out when `lastDemurrageEpoch` advances:\n```typescript\n    // In getAccount signature:\n    getAccount(id: string, forceDecayForMutation = false): LedgerAccount {\n        // ...\n        return this.applyDecay(account, this.getCurrentEpoch(), forceDecayForMutation);\n    }\n    \n    // In applyDecay:\n    private applyDecay(account: LedgerAccount, currentEpoch: number, force = false): LedgerAccount {\n        // ...\n        if (!force && this.decayEvents.length >= this.MAX_PENDING_DECAY_EVENTS) {\n            // ... defer\n        }\n        if (!force && decayedAmount <= 0.0001) return account;\n```\nAnd pass `forceDecayForMutation = true` when calling `getAccount()` within `transfer()` and `moveToCommons()`."
+  }
